<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). Its picture (architect 2026-10-12; the forward clock
     since 2026-10-17 late evening): Adwaita 3.22's clock with its back arrow
     turned forward, the caption's icon and the glyph Warp wears,
     assets/icons/adwaita-3.22/AppIcon.svg, rasterised ANTIALIASED by
     rsvg-convert (librsvg on the laptop; a vector, not pixel art) and
     centered over WHITE, FLAT (architect 2026-10-17): #FFFFFF, one color
     over the whole canvas, so the mask shows a white shape carrying the
     drawing (Windows Storm's caption start #800080 from 2026-10-16 until
     then, the Cool Edit case's 20 face-ramp bands under Midnight's Face
     from 2026-10-12 before it). An
     ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so
     no legacy ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/, BOTH written by
     tools/app_icon/gen_app_icon.sh (which also writes the Linux desktop icon,
     packaging/warptempo_gui.svg, the same drawing bare):
       ic_launcher_background.png  the full 108 dp canvas flat in #FFFFFF;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the drawing rendered at the 52 dp art size,
                                   centred on a transparent canvas of the
                                   density's full 108 dp.

     THE 66 dp SAFE ZONE: an adaptive foreground's art should sit inside the
     mask's guaranteed-visible inner circle, Android's own 66 dp of the 108 dp
     canvas. The 48-unit drawing at 52 dp square (13/12 dp a unit; architect
     2026-10-16, his pick off a 60 / 56 / 52 / 48 / 44 / 40 dp series on the
     glass: at 64 dp the art filled ~86 % of the launcher's visible tile and
     nearly touched its corners) puts the case about 68 % of the visible tile.
     The 52 dp square's own corners (half-diagonal 36.8 dp) lie outside the
     33 dp radius of that circle, but they are empty: the drawing's case is
     44 x 34 of its 48 units centered in them, 47.67 x 36.83 dp, whose
     corners lie 30.1 dp from the center, inside the circle with 2.9 dp to
     spare. The same 52 dp
     at every density (the per-density PNG pixel size scales with the density
     factor f alone):

       density  f    canvas C=108f  art 52f  offset (C-52f)/2
       mdpi     1    108            52       28
       hdpi     1.5  162            78       42
       xhdpi    2    216            104      56
       xxhdpi   3    324            156      84
       xxxhdpi  4    432            208      112

     A ONE-SHOT, NOT A BUILD STEP: the PNGs are rendered once on the laptop
     and committed; a change of the drawing or the ground is a re-run of the generator
     (bash tools/app_icon/gen_app_icon.sh, byte-stable), never a build step
     (build_apk.sh only compiles res/). -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
